# Nibs — agentic-first issue tracker

Track ALL work in this project with nibs (issues stored as Markdown files), not
TodoWrite or ad-hoc todo lists.

**Learn the CLI grammar first: run `nibs cheat` once.** It prints the whole
verb surface (get/list/rel, new/set/body/mv/rm/close, catalog) on one screen.
For detail: `nibs catalog <topic>` (fields, filters, hierarchy, recipes,
examples, schema) and `nibs <cmd> --help`. Full reference: `nibs prime --full`.
Do not guess syntax — read the grammar first.

## Workflow

- BEFORE a task: find or create a nib (`nibs list --ready`, `nibs new "Title" -t <type>`), set it `in-progress` (`nibs set <id> -s in-progress`).{{if .StartableStatuses}} `--ready` returns only unblocked nibs whose status is {{codes .StartableStatuses "/"}} — nothing else is startable.{{end}}{{if and .HoldingStatuses .ReleasingStatuses}} Note that a {{codes .HoldingStatuses "/"}} blocker still blocks — it is closed, but the work is coming back, so it does not release its dependents the way a {{codes .ReleasingStatuses "/"}} blocker does.{{end}}
- DURING: keep the body's todo items current (`- [ ]` → `- [x]`) as work happens (`nibs body <id> --replace-old … --replace-new …`).
- AFTER: close it only when no unchecked todos remain — `nibs close <id> --summary -` (writes a `## Summary`, propagates to the parent). `--as <closed status>` picks the close reason ({{join .ClosedStatuses "/"}}; {{.DefaultCloseStatus}} when omitted), so abandoned work is `nibs close <id> --as scrapped --summary -` and work set aside is `--as deferred`. `nibs set -s` refuses a closed status: closing an existing nib goes through `close`, because only `close` requires the summary that records why.
- COMMITS: include both code and nib files.
- SUBAGENTS: `nibs set <id> -s in-progress` BEFORE launching, `nibs close <id> --summary -` AFTER — they run fresh and won't update nibs for you.

## Errors

Every command uses stable exit codes (0 ok / 2 validation / 3 not-found / 4 conflict / 5 io); with `--json`, errors come back as `{"error":{"code","message"}}`. If a `nibs` command errors, STOP. Find the root cause and suggest a mitigation (code fix, follow-up nib, workaround). Never silently retry.
